body:
Cody has decided (2026-11-16) that no SisyphusMD job will run on GitHub-hosted runners. The macOS CI, the release builds and the install matrix all move to our own runners, and the GitHub mirrors stop running Actions.

Several shared helpers exist only to bridge to GitHub's runners, and they become dead weight once the product repos stop using them:
- `check-mirror-ci.sh`: waits for GitHub's ci-macos and formula-macos verdict on a SHA.
- `triage-infra-failure.py`: classifies failures for GitHub's retry-infra-failures workflow.
- `forgejo-preflight.sh`: lets GitHub-hosted runners probe for a CrowdSec ban on Forgejo.
- the GitHub half of `check-rc-install-matrix.sh`.

`macos-scope.sh` also has a gap: it treats every `.forgejo/` path as Linux-only. A Renovate branch that changes only `.forgejo/workflows/macos.yml` therefore skips the Mac run that would test that very change.

Wanted:
- a Forgejo-side gate that waits for a workflow's run on a SHA, replacing `check-mirror-ci.sh`;
- `check-rc-install-matrix.sh` reading the single Forgejo `install-matrix.yml` run for the candidate;
- the GitHub-only helpers and their tests retired;
- `macos-scope.sh` running the Mac whenever `a private repo.yml` changes;
- docs and VARIANCE updated to match.

On a private repo (2026-11-20) the AI review failed closed three times in a row on its own output, never on the diff:
- a ValueError;
- no JSON in the answer;
- `finding F5 has an invalid severity or status`.

`.forgejo/scripts/ai-review.py` (around line 243) raises on the first finding whose severity is not `blocking` or `suggestion`, so every other finding is thrown away along with the verdict and the PR stays blocked. Proposed: re-ask the model once with the validation error, and if it still fails, report the malformed finding as a blocking finding with its raw text, so the review still fails closed but the author can see and answer the findings. Includes a test that fails on today's code.

Closes #114

When the first review's answer can't be read or checked, the retry is now a restate instead of a second free review. The model gets its own rejected answer back (its text, and the end of its reasoning when the server returns it) and answers under a strict `json_schema` that mirrors what `validate` accepts, so the grammar rules out a wrong shape.

The first review stays unconstrained. Measured on the Studio, oMLX caps reasoning near 4,096 tokens under a schema (a long derivation stopped at 4,094), and reviews reason for over 20,000.

Also:
- a reply with no `choices` (a server error body) is a named ValueError and gets the retry, while a KeyError or TypeError from a broken script or setup still fails as an error, not as a malformed answer;
- a server that refuses `response_format` (a 400 or 422 that names the schema) gets the free re-ask, and any other 400, such as an over-long prompt, fails as before;
- the schema retry is capped at 16,000 output tokens, so both calls fit the deadline;
- long text is clipped keeping its start and end.

Checked live against the Studio (oMLX 0.8.2):
- the restate turned a prose-only rejected answer into a valid blocking finding in 5 to 12 seconds with 63 to 144 reasoning tokens;
- the schema is enforced with no Warning header (a requested severity `major` came back `suggestion`, and a blank id was forced to contain visible characters).

Tests: 17 new or changed; the new ones fail against the old script.
